import{_ as i,o as t,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 493 | Cross-IP Synthesis: Typology of Predatory Cultivation Systems — Five Predation Modes","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 493 | Cross-IP Synthesis: Typology of Predatory Cultivation Systems — Five Predation Modes","no":493,"module":2,"tags":["Cross-IP Synthesis","Predatory Cultivation","Typology","Five Modes","Anti-Predation"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis","05-Myriad-Ranks Joint-Advancement Basic Program","19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0493_模块2-跨IP综合-掠夺式修炼体系类型学-五种掠夺模式.md","filePath":"en/0493_模块2-跨IP综合-掠夺式修炼体系类型学-五种掠夺模式.md"}'),s={name:"en/0493_模块2-跨IP综合-掠夺式修炼体系类型学-五种掠夺模式.md"};function a(r,e,l,u,d,c){return t(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-493-cross-ip-synthesis-typology-of-predatory-cultivation-systems-—-five-predation-modes" tabindex="-1">Entry 493 | Cross-IP Synthesis: Typology of Predatory Cultivation Systems — Five Predation Modes <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-493-cross-ip-synthesis-typology-of-predatory-cultivation-systems-—-five-predation-modes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 493 | Cross-IP Synthesis: Typology of Predatory Cultivation Systems — Five Predation Modes&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Cross-IP Synthesis (Entry 2) | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 05, 19</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-predation-is-not-one-kind-it-has-five-faces" tabindex="-1">Introduction: predation is not one kind; it has five faces <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-predation-is-not-one-kind-it-has-five-faces" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: predation is not one kind; it has five faces&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou (Myriad-Spirits Balanced-Anchor Origin Universe)&#39;s six top-level axioms — anti-predation axiom, republican axiom of Myriad Races, collective ascension axiom, causal self-discipline axiom, <strong>law-first axiom</strong>, universal equal infinite law as core — through per-entry decomposition of Tang Luo (252–287), Ye Fan (288–301), Tang San / Douluo, Ji Ning (406–431), Wukong (432–467), Zheng Zha (468–477), Jackie Chan (478–484), Gu Chensha (485–491), summarizes five predation modes. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. They are not moral judgments, but <strong>structural classifications.</strong></p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-cross-ip-summary" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Cross-IP Summary) <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones-cross-ip-summary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones (Cross-IP Summary)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Five predation modes&#39; common waste: compressing energy that could have universally benefited Myriad Ranks into one person&#39;s or small circle&#39;s private property. The difference is only in &quot;the way of compression.&quot;</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-cross-ip-summary" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Cross-IP Summary) <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-cross-ip-summary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression (Cross-IP Summary)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Each predation mode has its own regression path; see Entry 496.</p><h2 id="iii-five-predation-modes-typology" tabindex="-1">III. Five Predation Modes Typology <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-five-predation-modes-typology" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Five Predation Modes Typology&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Predation Mode 1: Resource-Capture Type (Tang San / Douluo)</strong> — evolution path through slaughter, hunting, snatching spirit rings. Power comes from consuming stock.</li><li><strong>Predation Mode 2: Position-Monopoly Type (Ye Fan / Shrouding, Shi Hao / Perfect World)</strong> — monopolize Great Emperor / Supreme position; ten-thousand years of peace surnamed &quot;Ye&quot; or &quot;Shi.&quot; Power comes from institutional monopoly.</li><li><strong>Predation Mode 3: Origin-Burning Type (Zheng Zha / Infinite Terror Genetic Lock)</strong> — press one&#39;s own life potential to trade for power. Power comes from borrowing from future self.</li><li><strong>Predation Mode 4: Zero-Sum Contest Type (Jackie Chan Adventures Twelve Talismans)</strong> — repeatedly contest unreplicable zero-sum resources. Power comes from occupying position.</li><li><strong>Predation Mode 5: Gift-Bearing Type (Tang Luo, Gu Chensha)</strong> — bringing civilization&#39;s key functions back to one person; bearing everything for Myriad Ranks. Power comes from outsourcing subjectivity.</li></ol><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Predation Mode</th><th>Symbiotic Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Resource-Capture</td><td>Develop increment; do not consume stock (anti-predation axiom)</td></tr><tr><td>Position-Monopoly</td><td>Myriad-Ranks republicanism; anti-monopoly in constitution</td></tr><tr><td>Origin-Burning</td><td>Life-cycle system; energy grows naturally</td></tr><tr><td>Zero-Sum Contest</td><td>Principles publicized; zero-sum turns non-zero-sum</td></tr><tr><td>Gift-Bearing</td><td>Myriad Ranks bear themselves; subjectivity returned</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Quest Sediment Domain runs &quot;hundred-year simulations&quot; for five modes respectively: A Resource-Capture type after a hundred years civilization battle-loss heavy; B Position-Monopoly type after a hundred years class solidification; C Origin-Burning type after a hundred years strong ones collectively premature aging; D Zero-Sum Contest type after a hundred years spinning in place; E Gift-Bearing type after a hundred years Myriad-Ranks ability regression. Heng-Yuan-Zhou-type symbiosis after a hundred years, Myriad Ranks&#39; energy levels universally leap.</p><p>Five modes are not mutually exclusive; they often stack. Tang San&#39;s Douluo system is simultaneously A (hunting spirit beasts) and B (monopolizing spirit-master positions); Zheng Zha&#39;s Infinite Terror is simultaneously C (Genetic Lock burns life) and D (instance zero-sum); Gu Chensha&#39;s Dragon Rune is simultaneously E (gift-bearing) and B (monopolizing Tiandao Law). The heavier the stack, the more fragile civilization. What Heng Yuan Zhou needs is not eliminating one mode at a time, but fundamentally replacing the underlying logic of &quot;predatory cultivation&quot; — replaced with &quot;develop increment, do not consume stock,&quot; all five modes lose their soil.</p><p>Five predation modes&#39; deep commonality: they all understand &quot;cultivation&quot; as &quot;acquisition&quot; — acquire spirit rings, acquire position, acquire lifespan, acquire talismans, acquire gifts. Heng Yuan Zhou understands cultivation as &quot;growth&quot; — not acquiring external things, but developing internal abilities. This difference is fundamental: acquisition is zero-sum (you take more I take less), growth is non-zero-sum (my growth does not affect yours). Five predation modes all built on the wrong premise of &quot;cultivation = acquisition.&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s symbiotic cultivation is built on the correct premise of &quot;cultivation = growth.&quot; Premise changed, all five modes invalidate.</p><p>Five predation modes&#39; typology also has a practical use: it lets Heng Yuan Zhou when facing a new IP quickly judge &quot;which predation modes this IP falls into.&quot; Tang San falls into A+B; Zheng Zha falls into C+D; Gu Chensha falls into E+B; Tang Luo falls into E; Ye Fan falls into B. After judging which modes, directly invoke corresponding symbiotic alternatives. <strong>Typology is not academic classification; it is construction guide.</strong></p><p>Five predation modes&#39; summarization ultimately points to a Heng Yuan Zhou core belief: <strong>all predatory cultivation can be replaced by the same scheme — replicable, teachable, universalizable symbiotic cultivation system.</strong> The 300 Origin cultivation systems are this scheme&#39;s concrete implementation.</p><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Self-consistency law</strong>: the stronger the predation mode, the lower the setting self-consistency (because protagonist must continuously break through predation rules)</li><li><strong>Retcon risk law</strong>: all five modes accompanied by retcon, especially Resource-Capture and Origin-Burning</li><li><strong>Heng Yuan Zhou reference</strong>: the only cosmos not falling into any predation mode</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: all five modes compress universal-benefit energy into private property</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: five modes each have predation; Heng Yuan Zhou opposes all</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo belongs to the fifth (Gift-Bearing type), already the mildest among predatory schools</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: all five modes exclude 99% of Myriad Ranks</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: all five modes reverse to symbiotic cosmos</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predation is not one word; it is five structures. Heng Yuan Zhou opposes not &quot;protagonist getting strong,&quot; but &quot;the way protagonist gets strong.&quot; <strong>True evolution should let Myriad Ranks get strong together, not one person step on Myriad Ranks&#39; heads to get strong.</strong></p><p>In the final analysis, Cross-IP synthesis · predatory cultivation system typology · five predation modes described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./492_模块2-跨IP综合-主角唯一性依赖度五级标准总览.html">Entry 492 · Five-Level Standard</a> · <a href="./496_模块2-跨IP综合-文明倒退机制总分析-四种倒退路径.html">Entry 496 · Civilizational Regression Paths</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const y=i(s,[["render",a]]);export{m as __pageData,y as default};
